01:03:47.320 --> 01:03:48.820
Will you send me a ketchup chip?
你们能寄给我一片番茄酱薯片吗？

1700
01:03:48.820 --> 01:03:49.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1701
01:03:49.760 --> 01:03:50.260
Get ready.
准备好了。

1702
01:03:50.800 --> 01:03:53.120
But listen, make sure some come my way.
但听着，一定要留点给我。

1703
01:03:53.400 --> 01:03:54.060
You got it.
没问题。

1704
01:03:54.180 --> 01:03:54.900
They're tangy.
味道很浓郁。

1705
01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:55.580
They're delicious.
非常美味。

1706
01:03:56.280 --> 01:03:56.560
Okay.
好的。

1707
01:03:57.220 --> 01:03:59.000
Guess who else is at the bar?
猜猜还有谁在吧台？

1708
01:03:59.700 --> 01:04:00.560
Concierge Marie!
礼宾员玛丽！

1709
01:04:01.060 --> 01:04:01.340
Yeah!
没错！

1710
01:04:01.340 --> 01:04:05.220
Michael is, how you say, so excited to see her.
迈克尔怎么说呢，见到她非常兴奋。

1711
01:04:05.460 --> 01:04:05.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1712
01:04:06.260 --> 01:04:07.380
How do you say it?
你是怎么说的？

1713
01:04:07.540 --> 01:04:08.420
How do you say it?
你是怎么说的？

1714
01:04:08.880 --> 01:04:11.380
Andy's going to bring him two glasses of wine.
安迪打算给他拿两杯酒。

1715
01:04:11.740 --> 01:04:12.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1716
01:04:12.200 --> 01:04:13.540
He's going to get things started.
他打算把气氛搞起来。

1717
01:04:13.800 --> 01:04:14.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1718
01:04:14.160 --> 01:04:18.820
He's also going to try to get things started for Oscar and a couple of gentlemen sitting at a
他还打算帮奥斯卡和坐在旁边桌子的

1719
01:04:18.820 --> 01:04:19.520
table nearby.
几位男士也把气氛搞起来。

1720
01:04:19.840 --> 01:04:20.200
That's right.
没错。

1721
01:04:20.260 --> 01:04:21.420
He says to the bartender,
他对酒保说：

1722
01:04:22.120 --> 01:04:26.140
Mademoiselle, beer me, dose Long Island iced teas, see you play.
小姐，给我来两杯长岛冰茶，看你表现了。

1723
01:04:26.620 --> 01:04:28.120
Bad decision in a glass.
简直是装在杯子里的错误决定。

1724
01:04:28.440 --> 01:04:29.960
It is a bad decision in a glass.
确实是装在杯子里的错误决定。

1725
01:04:30.380 --> 01:04:31.200
It is a horrible decision.
那是个糟糕透顶的决定。

1726
01:04:31.340 --> 01:04:34.000
You know how you've had a volcano and you did the splits?
你记得你喝过火山鸡尾酒然后劈叉的事吗？

1727
01:04:34.260 --> 01:04:34.600
Yes.
记得。

1728
01:04:34.760 --> 01:04:36.620
I had some Long Island iced teas.
我喝过一些长岛冰茶。

1729
01:04:37.040 --> 01:04:37.560
Where?
在哪？

1730
01:04:37.840 --> 01:04:41.380
In the Bahamas on spring break with my friends.
在巴哈马，和朋友们过春假的时候。

1731
01:04:41.920 --> 01:04:43.780
I never had one before.
我以前从没喝过。

1732
01:04:44.140 --> 01:04:45.920
I wasn't 21 yet,
我当时还没满21岁，

1733
01:04:46.060 --> 01:04:48.100
but in the Bahamas, you can drink when you're 18.
但在巴哈马，18岁就可以喝酒了。

1734
01:04:48.560 --> 01:04:51.920
We went to the casino and they just give them
我们去了赌场，只要坐在老虎机前，

1735
01:04:51.920 --> 01:04:54.360
to you free if you sit at the slot machines.
他们就会免费给你提供。

1736
01:04:54.800 --> 01:04:57.580
All of this was like, what is happening?
当时这一切让我觉得，到底发生了什么？

1737
01:04:57.860 --> 01:04:59.780
I have not had a Long Island iced tea.
我还没喝过长岛冰茶。

1738
01:04:59.960 --> 01:05:00.780
I've had the volcano,
我喝过火山鸡尾酒，

1739
01:05:00.780 --> 01:05:02.060
but it's just the same thing.
但其实都一样。

1740
01:05:02.160 --> 01:05:03.720
They just dump a bunch of booze in it, right?
他们就是往里面倒了一堆酒，对吧？

1741
01:05:03.720 --> 01:05:05.780
It's like seven or eight different liquors.
里面混了七八种不同的烈酒。

1742
01:05:06.800 --> 01:05:07.200
Tasty.
好喝。

1743
01:05:07.440 --> 01:05:08.500
Went down easy.
喝起来很顺口。

1744
01:05:08.760 --> 01:05:09.260
Well, yeah.
嗯，确实。

1745
01:05:09.760 --> 01:05:10.840
Then a lot of vomiting.
然后就是一阵狂吐。

1746
01:05:11.040 --> 01:05:12.220
A lot of vomiting.
吐得一塌糊涂。

1747
01:05:12.220 --> 01:05:16.280
Well, we got a fan question about this scene from Evan L.
好了，我们收到一个关于这个场景的粉丝提问，来自埃文·L。

1748
01:05:16.820 --> 01:05:19.940
At 11 minutes, 14 seconds, Andy says,
在11分14秒时，安迪说：

1749
01:05:20.180 --> 01:05:22.380
you will thank me when they spank thee.
当她们打你屁股时，你会感谢我的。

1750
01:05:22.700 --> 01:05:25.400
And he wants to know who came up with that line.
他想知道这句台词是谁想出来的。

1751
01:05:25.400 --> 01:05:26.620
Can I guess?
我可以猜猜吗？

1752
01:05:26.780 --> 01:05:27.200
Sure.
当然。

1753
01:05:27.600 --> 01:05:28.180
Lee or Jean?
是李还是简？

1754
01:05:29.620 --> 01:05:31.040
That's a good guess.
猜得好。

1755
01:05:31.400 --> 01:05:35.760
It's in the script and I asked Brent Forrester about it and he said
剧本里有这句台词，我问过布伦特·福雷斯特，他说

1756
01:05:35.760 --> 01:05:40.240
he is the author of the thank me spank thee line.
那句“感谢我，打我屁股”的台词是他写的。

1757
01:05:40.720 --> 01:05:44.360
He said there are few things more fun than writing
他说没什么比给安迪这个角色写

1758
01:05:44.360 --> 01:05:46.980
a rhyming punchline for the Andy character.
押韵的俏皮话更有趣了。

1759
01:05:47.260 --> 01:05:50.420
He said he got a little bit too into writing
他说那一季他写

1760
01:05:50.420 --> 01:05:53.100
rhyming punchlines for Ed that season.
给艾德写的押韵俏皮话有点写上瘾了。

1761
01:05:53.360 --> 01:05:55.980
He said that one day in the writer's room,
他说有一天在编剧室里，

1762
01:05:56.100 --> 01:06:01.820
he pitched a line where Andy refers to his quote, backup snack pack backpack.
他提议让安迪提到他的什么“备用零食包背包”。

1763
01:06:02.920 --> 01:06:08.540
And he said at that point, the writers forbid him from writing any more rhyming punchlines for
他说从那以后，编剧们就禁止他再写任何押韵的俏皮话了，

1764
01:06:08.540 --> 01:06:09.260
the rest of the year.
在那一年剩下的时间里都不行。

1765
01:06:09.400 --> 01:06:11.760
I wonder if he wrote nifty gifties.
我在想“俏皮礼物”是不是也是他写的。

1766
01:06:12.180 --> 01:06:13.400
He might have.
没准是。

1767
01:06:13.520 --> 01:06:14.780
Oh, Brent, that's so good.
噢，布伦特，那太棒了。

1768
01:06:14.780 --> 01:06:17.400
Oh, well, guess what?
噢，好吧，你猜怎么着？

1769
01:06:17.860 --> 01:06:19.560
They're not going to spank him.
他们不会打他屁股的。

1770
01:06:19.800 --> 01:06:20.400
They're not.
他们没打。

1771
01:06:20.680 --> 01:06:21.620
They turn him down.
他们拒绝了他。

1772
01:06:21.900 --> 01:06:26.480
And Oscar and Andy now drink the Long Island iced teas, which is going to lead to some trouble.
奥斯卡和安迪现在喝起了长岛冰茶，这要惹出麻烦了。

1773
01:06:26.720 --> 01:06:32.720
Some real trouble because Oscar says to Andy, what do you see in Angela?
真的麻烦，因为奥斯卡问安迪：你到底看上安吉拉哪一点？

1774
01:06:33.100 --> 01:06:35.380
And again, I was hungry as I watched this.
再说一次，我看这段的时候肚子饿了。

1775
01:06:35.600 --> 01:06:39.320
So at 12 minutes, 17 seconds, I can see another bag of
所以在12分17秒的时候，我看到另一袋

1776
01:06:39.320 --> 01:06:43.100
old Dutch potato chips sitting next to Oscar's arm on the bar.
老荷兰牌薯片放在吧台奥斯卡的手臂旁边。

1777
01:06:43.240 --> 01:06:44.560
They're the green and white bag.
是那个绿白相间的袋子。

1778
01:06:44.560 --> 01:06:45.480
You know what that means.
你知道那意味着什么吗？

1779
01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:46.660
Sour cream and onion?
酸奶油洋葱味？

1780
01:06:46.960 --> 01:06:48.940
They are the dill pickle chips.
是酸黄瓜味的薯片。

1781
01:06:49.100 --> 01:06:49.320
What?
什么？

1782
01:06:49.960 --> 01:06:50.400
Yep.
没错。

1783
01:06:51.120 --> 01:06:52.100
Described on the internet.
网上有描述。

1784
01:06:52.160 --> 01:06:53.820
Do they make any regular flavors?
他们家出普通口味的吗？

1785
01:06:54.440 --> 01:06:55.120
They do.
有的。

1786
01:06:55.280 --> 01:06:57.300
I'm telling you, these chips are so good.
我跟你说，这些薯片太好吃了。

1787
01:06:57.580 --> 01:06:59.280
You've had the dill pickle ones?
你吃过酸黄瓜味的？

1788
01:06:59.440 --> 01:07:00.440
I have sampled.
我尝过。

1789
01:07:00.640 --> 01:07:03.760
You know, like on set, we would have a whole bunch of bags of chips.
你知道，在片场，我们会有好几袋薯片。

1790
01:07:05.040 --> 01:07:06.620
They're real salty and I liked it.
它们真的很咸，我喜欢。

1791
01:07:06.620 --> 01:07:08.560
I guess I'm a chip traditionaliSt.
我想我是一个薯片传统主义者。

1792
01:07:08.840 --> 01:07:09.400
You know what?
你知道吗？

1793
01:07:09.400 --> 01:07:10.640
You need to be a chip traveler.
你需要做一个薯片旅行者。

1794
01:07:11.020 --> 01:07:11.500
All right.
好吧。

1795
01:07:11.720 --> 01:07:13.780
You need to try some international chips.
你需要尝试一些国际口味的薯片。

1796
01:07:13.780 --> 01:07:14.720
I'll try them.
我会试试的。

1797
01:07:14.900 --> 01:07:16.420
Well, the dill ones are real salty.
嗯，酸黄瓜味的真的很咸。

1798
01:07:17.720 --> 01:07:19.140
I do like a pickle.
我确实喜欢酸黄瓜。

1799
01:07:19.360 --> 01:07:19.900
I know.
我知道。

1800
01:07:20.500 --> 01:07:24.820
But anyway, Andy drunk dials Angela.
但不管怎样，安迪喝醉后给安吉拉打了电话。

1801
01:07:25.100 --> 01:07:26.940
This is a huge mistake.
这真是个大错特错的决定。

1802
01:07:27.160 --> 01:07:27.920
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

1803
01:07:27.940 --> 01:07:29.000
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1804
01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:30.160
We're going to discuss this.
我们要讨论一下这件事。

1805
01:07:30.300 --> 01:07:31.980
We will discuss this naked.
我们要赤身裸体地讨论这件事。

1806
01:07:32.380 --> 01:07:34.600
But then there's a voice in the background.
但随后背景里有个声音。

1807
01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:37.540
I mean, she's with Dwight.
我是说，她和德怀特在一起。

1808
01:07:37.540 --> 01:07:38.880
Of course she is.
当然是这样。

1809
01:07:39.320 --> 01:07:39.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1810
01:07:39.800 --> 01:07:43.860
But somehow Andy doesn't totally register it.
但安迪不知怎么地没完全意识到这一点。

1811
01:07:43.920 --> 01:07:45.580
He's had a Long Island iced tea.
他喝了一杯长岛冰茶。

1812
01:07:45.920 --> 01:07:47.220
Several, I think, at this point.
我想这会儿已经喝了好几杯了。

1813
01:07:47.380 --> 01:07:47.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1814
01:07:47.940 --> 01:07:49.280
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1815
01:07:49.380 --> 01:07:51.820
Michael and Concierge Marie, they're clicking.
迈克尔和礼宾员玛丽，他们很合得来。

1816
01:07:52.180 --> 01:07:53.300
They're going to leave.
他们要离开了。

1817
01:07:53.540 --> 01:07:56.200
They're going to smooch outside in the alley.
他们要去外面的小巷里亲热。

1818
01:07:56.200 --> 01:08:00.160
And we asked Wendy about this, about kissing Steve.
我们问了温迪关于这件事，关于亲吻史蒂夫的事。

1819
01:08:00.340 --> 01:08:01.520
And here's what she had to say.
以下是她的回答。

1820
01:08:01.880 --> 01:08:06.640
I was super nervous to kiss Steve Carell.
亲吻史蒂夫·卡瑞尔让我超级紧张。

1821
01:08:06.820 --> 01:08:12.560
I was so nervous that I was practically going into convulsions.
我紧张到几乎要抽搐了。

1822
01:08:13.080 --> 01:08:17.220
But I did it, and it was great, and I highly recommend it.
但我还是做了，感觉很棒，我强烈推荐。

1823
01:08:19.180 --> 01:08:20.700
She highly recommends.
她强烈推荐。

1824
01:08:21.020 --> 01:08:21.560
Oh, well.
哦，好吧。

1825
01:08:21.760 --> 01:08:24.060
They're not just going to kiss outside the hotel.
他们可不只是在酒店外面亲吻那么简单。

1826
01:08:24.320 --> 01:08:24.960
All right?
好吗？

1827
01:08:25.100 --> 01:08:30.060
We are going to cut to Michael being sort of shoved out of her.
我们要剪辑到迈克尔被从她房间里推出来的画面。

1828
01:08:30.320 --> 01:08:31.660
Room 887.
887号房。

1829
01:08:32.180 --> 01:08:32.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1830
01:08:32.800 --> 01:08:34.000
Without his shoes.
没穿鞋。

1831
01:08:34.240 --> 01:08:34.680
Barefoot.
光着脚。

1832
01:08:34.840 --> 01:08:36.100
He's shuffling down the hall.
他在走廊里拖着步子走。

1833
01:08:36.420 --> 01:08:36.880
I know.
我知道。

1834
01:08:37.120 --> 01:08:38.840
And then she's like, wait, you forgot your shoes.
然后她就像是，等等，你忘了你的鞋子了。

1835
01:08:38.840 --> 01:08:39.800
Only she says nothing.
只不过她什么也没说。

1836
01:08:39.800 --> 01:08:42.440
She just sets them out and quickly shuts the door.
她只是把鞋放出来，然后迅速关上了门。

1837
01:08:43.240 --> 01:08:46.040
Well, that kind of wraps up Concierge Marie.
好吧，礼宾员玛丽的故事就到此为止了。

1838
01:08:46.540 --> 01:08:51.820
We had to ask Wendy if she ever gets recognized for being on the show.
我们不得不问温迪，她是否因为出演这部剧而被认出来过。

1839
01:08:51.940 --> 01:08:52.940
And here's what she said.
以下是她的回答。

1840
01:08:53.400 --> 01:08:53.880
Yes.
是的。

1841
01:08:54.460 --> 01:08:55.660
So many times.
很多次。

1842
01:08:55.660 --> 01:08:59.920
I'm so surprised at that because I was, you know, barely in it.
我对此感到非常惊讶，因为你知道，我几乎没怎么出镜。

1843
01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:04.580
But, you know, that just speaks to the reach and the popularity of the office.
但你知道，这恰恰说明了《办公室》的影响力和受欢迎程度。

1844
01:09:05.300 --> 01:09:07.060
I read a fun fact about Wendy.
我读到过一个关于温迪的趣事。

1845
01:09:07.400 --> 01:09:08.180
Yes, you did.
是的，你读过。

1846
01:09:08.320 --> 01:09:08.780
Share it, Jenna.
分享一下吧，珍娜。

1847
01:09:08.900 --> 01:09:09.480
It's so good.
太棒了。

1848
01:09:09.480 --> 01:09:09.960
Okay.
好的。

1849
01:09:10.440 --> 01:09:17.840
Wendy was the editor for California State University's Academic Journal of Social Work.
温迪曾是加州州立大学《社会工作学术期刊》的编辑。

1850
01:09:18.060 --> 01:09:21.140
This was her day job before she hit it big as an actress.
这是她在作为演员成名之前的工作。

1851
01:09:21.140 --> 01:09:28.380
But even after she was working all the time, she kept her job until 2012.
但即便在工作排得满满当当之后，她还是保留了那份工作直到2012年。

1852
01:09:29.180 --> 01:09:31.740
Bridesmaids came out in 2011.
《伴娘》是在2011年上映的。

1853
01:09:31.740 --> 01:09:36.900
So even after Bridesmaids, she was still editing this journal of social work.
所以即使在《伴娘》之后，她依然在编辑这份社会工作期刊。

1854
01:09:37.020 --> 01:09:38.840
And we had to ask her about it.
我们不得不问问她这件事。

1855
01:09:39.040 --> 01:09:39.960
Here's what she said.
她是这么说的。

1856
01:09:39.960 --> 01:09:50.300
It is true that while I was building my acting career and, you know, doing pretty well, that I kept my side job at Cal State Long Beach.
确实，在我发展演艺事业并且做得还不错的时候，我依然保留了在加州州立大学长滩分校的副业。

1857
01:09:50.300 --> 01:09:54.920
I was an assistant editor for a social work journal.
我当时是一家社会工作期刊的助理编辑。

1858
01:09:55.180 --> 01:10:05.040
I did that for 12 years, all through Reno 911, all through, you know, all these movies that I did, Rules of Engagement, and right up until the Goldbergs.
我做了12年，贯穿了整个《雷诺911》，贯穿了，你知道的，我拍的所有这些电影，比如《聘妻记》，一直到《戈德堡一家》。

1859
01:10:05.160 --> 01:10:09.800
And the only reason I'm not doing it anymore is because the journal folded.
我不再做这份工作的唯一原因就是期刊停刊了。

1860
01:10:09.800 --> 01:10:14.000
It went out of business, but it was a great job.
它倒闭了，但那真的是一份很棒的工作。

1861
01:10:14.160 --> 01:10:16.560
It was, like, not even 20 hours a week.
每周工作时间甚至不到20个小时。

1862
01:10:16.560 --> 01:10:18.820
I could do it from wherever I was.
无论我在哪里都能做。

1863
01:10:18.940 --> 01:10:22.500
And it was all about, you know, people in the social work profession.
而且内容全是关于，你知道的，社会工作行业的人们。

1864
01:10:22.500 --> 01:10:27.140
And let's be honest, those people deserve a lot of credit for what they do.
说实话，这些人所做的工作值得我们给予高度赞扬。

1865
01:10:27.280 --> 01:10:28.560
They don't get recognized enough.
他们得到的认可还不够多。

1866
01:10:28.980 --> 01:10:29.920
Yeah, it was great.
是的，那真的很棒。

1867
01:10:29.920 --> 01:10:31.440
And I loved doing it.
我热爱那份工作。

1868
01:10:31.520 --> 01:10:36.820
I loved my original boss who used to come and see my shows at the Groundlings.
我喜欢我最初的老板，她以前常来看我在Groundlings的演出。

1869
01:10:36.820 --> 01:10:40.900
Like, she was just so super supportive that she said, please don't ever quit.
她真的非常支持我，甚至跟我说，请千万别辞职。

1870
01:10:40.900 --> 01:10:44.780
So I kept my word, and I stayed until the very end.
所以我信守承诺，一直坚持到了最后。

1871
01:10:45.320 --> 01:10:47.760
See what I was saying about amazing human being?
看吧，我说的了不起的人就是这样。

1872
01:10:48.000 --> 01:10:48.880
I love her.
我爱她。

1873
01:10:49.160 --> 01:10:51.380
You know, that was so moving to me when I heard it.
你知道，当我听到这些时，真的非常感动。

1874
01:10:51.600 --> 01:10:53.220
My niece is a social worker.
我的侄女就是一名社会工作者。

1875
01:10:54.120 --> 01:11:01.480
I'm just always, you know, honestly, guys, I'm lifting her up in prayer all the time because it's not an easy job.
我总是，你知道的，老实说，伙计们，我一直在为她祈祷，因为那不是一份轻松的工作。

1876
01:11:01.640 --> 01:11:05.800
And I'm thankful that we have people that have a passion for helping others in that way.
我很感激有这样一群人，他们热衷于以那种方式帮助他人。

1877
01:11:05.800 --> 01:11:11.400
Yeah, it's not an easy job because sometimes you have to see and confront real hard things.
是的，那确实不容易，因为有时你必须面对和处理非常棘手的事情。

1878
01:11:11.600 --> 01:11:11.760
Yes.
没错。

1879
01:11:12.180 --> 01:11:13.900
And then you have to hold that.
而且你还得承受这些。

1880
01:11:14.200 --> 01:11:14.460
Yeah.
是的。

1881
01:11:15.040 --> 01:11:15.300
Yeah.
没错。

1882
01:11:15.820 --> 01:11:25.060
Well, as if you needed another reason to love Wendy, I would also like to share that in 2009, 2010, and 2011,
好吧，如果说你还需要另一个爱温迪的理由，我还想分享的是，在2009年、2010年和2011年，

1883
01:11:25.840 --> 01:11:30.920
she rang in the New Year, performing at military bases in Iraq and Kuwait.
她是在伊拉克和科威特的军事基地表演中迎接新年的。

1884
01:11:31.240 --> 01:11:36.420
And she went to the smaller bases that a lot of people didn't go to that kind of rarely get entertainment.
她去了很多很少有人去、几乎没有娱乐活动的偏远小基地。

1885
01:11:37.100 --> 01:11:37.680
Love that.
太棒了。

1886
01:11:37.880 --> 01:11:38.520
Love you.
爱你。

1887
01:11:38.680 --> 01:11:39.200
Wendy.
温迪。

1888
01:11:39.800 --> 01:11:40.760
Thank you so much.
非常感谢你。

1889
01:11:40.820 --> 01:11:42.440
It was so great to reconnect with you.
能和你重新联系上真是太好了。

1890
01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:44.720
Thanks for sharing your memories of the office.
感谢你分享关于办公室的回忆。

1891
01:11:44.960 --> 01:11:47.680
You guys, you can find Wendy in so many places.
大家，你们可以在很多地方找到温迪。

1892
01:11:47.680 --> 01:11:48.700
She's so talented.
她非常有才华。

1893
01:11:48.960 --> 01:11:51.600
She has a podcast called Generation Ripe.
她有一个播客叫《Generation Ripe》。

1894
01:11:51.860 --> 01:11:54.200
It is for teenagers over 40.
那是为40岁以上的“青少年”准备的。

1895
01:11:54.780 --> 01:12:00.960
It's described as a Generation Ripe listener is someone who thinks of their age as an asset, not a liability.
它的描述是：Generation Ripe的听众是将年龄视为资产而非负担的人。

1896
01:12:01.280 --> 01:12:05.140
We are older people with young souls are younger people with old souls.
我们是拥有年轻灵魂的老年人，或者是拥有老灵魂的年轻人。

1897
01:12:05.700 --> 01:12:07.540
Of course, she's on the Goldbergs.
当然，她还在演《戈德堡一家》。

1898
01:12:07.640 --> 01:12:09.020
They're about to start season nine.
他们马上就要开始第九季了。

1899
01:12:09.300 --> 01:12:14.660
She's on a Marvel series on Hulu called Modak and just tons of other things, you guys.
她还在Hulu的漫威剧集《魔多客》里出演，还有其他一大堆作品，伙计们。

1900
01:12:14.820 --> 01:12:19.060
And you can find her on Instagram at Wendy McClendon Covey.
你们可以在Instagram上关注她，账号是Wendy McClendon Covey。

1901
01:12:20.040 --> 01:12:20.820
Let's see.
让我看看。

1902
01:12:20.980 --> 01:12:21.980
Where should we go?
我们该去哪儿呢？

1903
01:12:22.120 --> 01:12:23.600
It's the next day.
第二天了。

1904
01:12:24.200 --> 01:12:25.740
Oh, people are hungover.
噢，大家宿醉了。

1905
01:12:25.900 --> 01:12:27.200
Very hungover.
宿醉得很厉害。

1906
01:12:27.980 --> 01:12:30.820
Andy does not remember calling Angela.
安迪不记得给安吉拉打过电话。

1907
01:12:31.120 --> 01:12:32.020
I know.
我知道。

1908
01:12:32.440 --> 01:12:33.140
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1909
01:12:33.960 --> 01:12:34.440
Oh.
噢。

1910
01:12:34.700 --> 01:12:37.300
Michael is very melancholy.
迈克尔非常忧郁。

1911
01:12:37.560 --> 01:12:37.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1912
01:12:37.800 --> 01:12:43.560
And he has to go sell paper at Catalyst Paper, which I looked it up.
而且他得去Catalyst Paper卖纸，我查过了。

1913
01:12:43.720 --> 01:12:43.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1914
01:12:44.460 --> 01:12:53.800
It's a real Canadian paper company, but it looks like its headquarters is based in Richmond, British Columbia, which is over on the West CoaSt.
那是一家真正的加拿大造纸公司，但看起来总部在不列颠哥伦比亚省的列治文，那是在西海岸。

1915
01:12:54.100 --> 01:12:56.640
I could not find a Winnipeg branch.
我没找到温尼伯分部。

1916
01:12:56.920 --> 01:12:59.300
I mean, if you couldn't, I doubt it's there.
我是说，如果你都找不到，那估计就不存在。

1917
01:12:59.300 --> 01:13:03.820
David Wallace calls to congratulate Michael because he did it.
大卫·华莱士打电话来祝贺迈克尔，因为他成功了。

1918
01:13:04.000 --> 01:13:04.960
He got the sale.
他拿下了那笔订单。

1919
01:13:05.560 --> 01:13:07.020
Michael is mad.
迈克尔很生气。

1920
01:13:07.300 --> 01:13:13.700
Yeah, because he's realized that this trip was a band-aid to try to help his feelings about Holly being transferred.
是啊，因为他意识到这次旅行只是为了缓解他对于霍莉被调走而产生的失落感，就像创可贴一样。

1921
01:13:13.960 --> 01:13:14.920
He's upset.
他很难过。

1922
01:13:14.920 --> 01:13:16.600
And he tells him off.
于是他把对方臭骂了一顿。

1923
01:13:16.740 --> 01:13:16.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1924
01:13:17.200 --> 01:13:18.920
I have a location breakdown.
我有一份外景拍摄明细。

1925
01:13:19.880 --> 01:13:21.200
Why do you say it like that?
你为什么要那样说？

1926
01:13:21.580 --> 01:13:22.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

1927
01:13:22.440 --> 01:13:23.380
You said it like sad sack.
你刚才说得像个丧气鬼一样。

1928
01:13:23.620 --> 01:13:24.600
You said it like this.
你是这样说的。

1929
01:13:24.720 --> 01:13:26.360
I have a location breakdown.
我有一份外景拍摄明细。

1930
01:13:26.360 --> 01:13:28.040
Well, I'm sad with Michael.
好吧，我是在为迈克尔感到难过。

1931
01:13:28.340 --> 01:13:28.620
Aw.
噢。

1932
01:13:28.960 --> 01:13:29.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1933
01:13:29.640 --> 01:13:33.940
For the Winnipeg Airport for these scenes, we used Terminal No.
这些场景里的温尼伯机场，我们用的是洛杉矶国际机场的2号航站楼。

1934
01:13:34.100 --> 01:13:35.700
2 at LAX.
2号航站楼。

1935
01:13:36.040 --> 01:13:43.760
Randy let me know that there was an area that was out of service at that time and that our location manager, Kyle Alexander,
兰迪告诉我，当时那里有一个区域处于停用状态，我们的外景经理凯尔·亚历山大，

1936
01:13:44.260 --> 01:13:48.360
was able to get an agreement from the LAX airport to let us film there.
成功与洛杉矶机场达成协议，让我们在那里拍摄。

1937
01:13:48.580 --> 01:13:49.800
That's like unheard of.
这简直闻所未闻。

1938
01:13:49.940 --> 01:13:52.040
Well, LAX does not let you film.
是啊，洛杉矶机场通常不让人拍摄。

1939
01:13:52.240 --> 01:13:53.040
Like, they are hardcore.
他们非常强硬。

1940
01:13:53.040 --> 01:13:58.480
Well, especially after 9-11, they had incredibly strict airport security.
尤其是911之后，他们的机场安保极其严格。

1941
01:13:58.700 --> 01:14:04.760
So we were only allowed a very small number of cast and crew and extras.
所以我们只被允许带极少数的演职人员和群众演员。

1942
01:14:05.140 --> 01:14:10.640
Everybody had to submit credentials very far in advance and had to be screened.
每个人都必须提前很久提交证件并接受审查。

1943
01:14:10.760 --> 01:14:14.660
So he said they had to create what they called a micro unit.
所以他说他们必须组建一个所谓的微型摄制组。

1944
01:14:15.180 --> 01:14:16.760
That's how small it was.
规模就是那么小。

1945
01:14:16.960 --> 01:14:22.440
He said that the airplanes outside the window were not Air Canada planes.
他说窗外的飞机并不是加拿大航空的飞机。

1946
01:14:23.040 --> 01:14:29.240
They had to paint over the logos using visual effects during post-production.
他们必须在后期制作中通过视觉特效把标志涂掉。

1947
01:14:29.240 --> 01:14:33.080
And so they put the red maple leaf on the tail of one of the planes.
于是他们在其中一架飞机的尾部画上了红枫叶。

1948
01:14:33.620 --> 01:14:35.660
We could only afford to do one plane.
我们只负担得起处理一架飞机。

1949
01:14:36.040 --> 01:14:38.820
If you look over Michael's shoulder, it's on the left.
如果你看向迈克尔的肩膀那边，它就在左边。

1950
01:14:38.940 --> 01:14:39.760
Yeah, I saw it.
是啊，我看到了。

1951
01:14:40.580 --> 01:14:48.900
Well, before we get to this big business with Jim and Pam, we should probably let you know that Kelly is going to break up with Daryl.
在聊吉姆和帕姆的大事之前，我们得先告诉你们，凯莉要和达里尔分手了。

1952
01:14:49.320 --> 01:14:51.440
I mean, Ryan has a text ready to go.
我的意思是，瑞安已经写好了一条短信。

1953
01:14:51.540 --> 01:14:53.100
They just have to hit send together.
他们只需要一起按下发送键就行了。

1954
01:14:53.520 --> 01:14:55.740
And I think, what does Ryan want?
我在想，瑞安到底想要什么？

1955
01:14:55.880 --> 01:14:58.460
Does he want Daryl to come upstairs and make a scene?
他想让达里尔冲上楼来大闹一场吗？

1956
01:14:58.640 --> 01:14:59.700
What does Ryan want?
瑞安到底想要什么？

1957
01:14:59.860 --> 01:15:02.160
He wants to be the other guy.
他想当那个第三者。

1958
01:15:02.160 --> 01:15:05.360
Yeah, he wants a reaction out of Daryl.
没错，他想看到达里尔的反应。

1959
01:15:05.660 --> 01:15:07.440
Daryl seems relieved.
达里尔看起来如释重负。

1960
01:15:07.440 --> 01:15:09.940
He's whistling as he walks to his car.
他吹着口哨走向自己的车。

1961
01:15:10.120 --> 01:15:11.880
He responds immediately, okay, cool.
他立刻回复说，好的，酷。

1962
01:15:11.880 --> 01:15:15.300
And then literally is like doing a dance to his pickup truck.
然后简直是一路跳着舞走向他的皮卡车。

1963
01:15:15.480 --> 01:15:15.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1964
01:15:15.880 --> 01:15:18.420
He's like, whew, thank you, Ryan.
他就像在说，呼，谢谢你，瑞安。

1965
01:15:18.780 --> 01:15:23.880
And that then, of course, immediately makes Ryan less interested in this relationship.
当然，这立刻让瑞安对这段关系没那么感兴趣了。

1966
01:15:24.140 --> 01:15:24.720
And here we go.
我们要开始了。

1967
01:15:24.880 --> 01:15:25.380
And they're back.
他们回来了。

1968
01:15:25.380 --> 01:15:25.780
Here we go.
开始了。

1969
01:15:26.660 --> 01:15:27.420
All right.
好吧。

1970
01:15:27.860 --> 01:15:29.320
Jim is going to leave.
吉姆要离开了。

1971
01:15:29.320 --> 01:15:33.440
And again, you guys have this Jim and Pam scene at that golden hour.
再说一次，你们在黄金时刻拍了这场吉姆和帕姆的戏。

1972
01:15:33.840 --> 01:15:36.280
Your hair is sparkling with sunshine.
你的头发在阳光下闪闪发光。

1973
01:15:36.760 --> 01:15:39.360
It's like that sunset scene in the parking lot.
就像停车场那场日落戏一样。

1974
01:15:39.460 --> 01:15:40.520
You couldn't look cuter.
你看起来可爱极了。

1975
01:15:40.780 --> 01:15:41.360
I know.
我知道。

1976
01:15:41.540 --> 01:15:43.580
I thought this scene was really sweet.
我觉得这场戏真的很甜。

1977
01:15:44.180 --> 01:15:44.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1978
01:15:44.780 --> 01:15:47.120
Pam is standing in the parking lot.
帕姆站在停车场里。

1979
01:15:47.300 --> 01:15:49.540
And Jim says, what are you doing here?
吉姆问她，你在这里做什么？

1980
01:15:49.900 --> 01:15:54.780
Because he had told her on the phone, when you come back, you're going to come back the right way.
因为他在电话里告诉过她，等你回来时，你要以正确的方式回来。

1981
01:15:55.060 --> 01:15:55.400
Right.
没错。

1982
01:15:55.500 --> 01:15:56.240
And he's supportive.
而且他很支持她。

1983
01:15:56.240 --> 01:15:58.980
If she wants to take the class again, they'll get through it.
如果她想重修那门课，他们会一起克服的。

1984
01:15:58.980 --> 01:15:59.260
Yes.
是的。

1985
01:15:59.400 --> 01:16:04.680
That the right way to come back is for her to come back having graduated from art school.
所谓正确的回归方式，就是让她从艺术学校毕业后再回来。

1986
01:16:05.100 --> 01:16:06.680
So Pam's standing there.
所以帕姆站在那里。

1987
01:16:06.680 --> 01:16:09.520
And she says, I'm coming back the wrong way.
她说，我是以错误的方式回来的。

1988
01:16:09.860 --> 01:16:11.400
But she's OK with it.
但她对此没意见。

1989
01:16:11.460 --> 01:16:12.660
She's happy about it.
她对此感到很高兴。

1990
01:16:12.780 --> 01:16:13.920
She missed Scranton.
她想念斯克兰顿了。

1991
01:16:14.080 --> 01:16:14.820
She missed Jim.
她想念吉姆了。

1992
01:16:15.160 --> 01:16:18.580
She actually hated the graphic design school.
她其实很讨厌那所平面设计学校。

1993
01:16:19.040 --> 01:16:19.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1994
01:16:19.740 --> 01:16:23.340
She tells Jim, this isn't really what I wanted to do.
她告诉吉姆，这并不是我真正想做的事。

1995
01:16:23.480 --> 01:16:25.380
But she had to go to find that out.
但她必须去尝试才能发现这一点。

1996
01:16:25.520 --> 01:16:26.120
She did.
确实如此。

1997
01:16:26.120 --> 01:16:28.800
You know, we had a question from Evan L.
我们收到了埃文·L的一个问题。

1998
01:16:29.020 --> 01:16:32.460
Why did the writers have Pam fail art school?
为什么编剧要让帕姆在艺术学校挂科？

1999
01:16:32.760 --> 01:16:34.260
Well, that's a good question, Evan.
嗯，这是个好问题，埃文。

2000
01:16:34.700 --> 01:16:36.720
I asked Brent Forrester about it.
我问过布伦特·福雷斯特关于这件事的原因。

2001
01:16:36.840 --> 01:16:44.740
He said that the story of Pam failing art school and coming back, quote, the wrong way, was a pitch from Jen Salata.
他说帕姆艺术学校没毕业就回来，也就是所谓的“走错路”的故事，是简·萨拉塔提出的点子。

2002
01:16:45.280 --> 01:16:47.580
Brent said, I have a daughter.
布伦特说，我有个女儿。

2003
01:16:47.580 --> 01:16:50.520
And he said, I'm a big, fat feminiSt.
他说，我是个彻头彻尾的女权主义者。

2004
01:16:50.620 --> 01:16:51.440
That's a quote.
这是原话。

2005
01:16:51.980 --> 01:16:57.760
And the idea that Pam would give up on her dreams to be with a man really rubbed him the wrong way.
他觉得帕姆为了一个男人放弃梦想的设定让他非常不舒服。

2006
01:16:57.760 --> 01:17:05.860
But that Jen Salata absolutely insisted that the romantic power of this gesture outweighed any politics.
但简·萨拉塔坚持认为，这种浪漫举动的力量胜过任何政治考量。

2007
01:17:05.860 --> 01:17:19.960
And also that the truth for Pam was not that she was giving up on her dreams for Jim, but that she was distinguishing what her real dreams were.
而且帕姆的真相并非为了吉姆放弃梦想，而是她认清了自己真正的梦想是什么。

2008
01:17:19.960 --> 01:17:31.600
And I really liked that because I think what Pam did here in going to graphic design school was that she was taking her real dream of being a creative artiSt.
我真的很喜欢这一点，因为我觉得帕姆去读平面设计学校，其实是在追求她作为创意艺术家的真正梦想。

2009
01:17:31.600 --> 01:17:37.840
And she was doing what a lot of artists do, and she was trying to find a practical application.
她做了很多艺术家都会做的事，试图寻找一种实际的应用方式。

2010
01:17:38.440 --> 01:17:38.580
Right.
没错。

2011
01:17:38.700 --> 01:17:40.660
How can I sort of do art but make a living?
我该怎么做艺术又能维持生计呢？

2012
01:17:40.840 --> 01:17:41.160
Yeah.
是啊。

2013
01:17:41.240 --> 01:17:41.420
Right?
对吧？

2014
01:17:41.720 --> 01:17:42.920
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

2015
01:17:43.280 --> 01:17:49.120
But, you know, I mean, people go into graphic design when they're passionate about graphic design.
但你知道，人们从事平面设计是因为他们热爱平面设计。

2016
01:17:49.200 --> 01:17:51.300
It's not some backup job, right?
那不是什么备选工作，对吧？

2017
01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:56.580
And the truth is, is that Pam discovered she does not have a passion for graphic design.
事实是，帕姆发现她对平面设计并没有热情。

2018
01:17:56.580 --> 01:18:02.140
And that's sort of what I had in my head when I was doing that scene on the phone with Jim and Pam's crying.
我在拍那场吉姆和帕姆通电话、帕姆哭泣的戏时，脑子里想的就是这些。

2019
01:18:02.640 --> 01:18:07.420
Pam is realizing that even if she did pass the course, this isn't for her.
帕姆意识到即使她通过了课程，这也不适合她。

2020
01:18:07.900 --> 01:18:10.200
But she's also embarrassed that she failed.
但她也为自己的失败感到尴尬。

2021
01:18:10.900 --> 01:18:17.540
But what she definitely does not want to do is spend 12 more weeks studying something she doesn't love.
但她绝对不想再花12周去学习她不热爱的东西。

2022
01:18:17.880 --> 01:18:22.080
For me in that moment, I just saw Pam stating her truth.
对我来说，那一刻我只看到帕姆在陈述她的真相。

2023
01:18:22.300 --> 01:18:24.480
And I always think that's so powerful.
我一直觉得那非常有力量。

2024
01:18:24.960 --> 01:18:25.120
Yeah.
是啊。

2025
01:18:25.120 --> 01:18:29.860
There is a very sweet deleted scene, you guys, with Jim and Pam.
伙计们，有一个非常温馨的删减片段，是关于吉姆和帕姆的。

2026
01:18:30.080 --> 01:18:31.360
It's in the break room.
是在休息室里。

2027
01:18:31.520 --> 01:18:32.540
And you know what?
你知道吗？

2028
01:18:32.640 --> 01:18:33.540
I'm titling it.
我给它起了个标题。

2029
01:18:33.820 --> 01:18:34.240
What?
什么？

2030
01:18:34.480 --> 01:18:35.720
Love in the break room.
休息室里的爱。

2031
01:18:35.980 --> 01:18:36.920
What is it?
是什么？

2032
01:18:37.460 --> 01:18:39.880
Pam is showing Jim her art assignment.
帕姆在给吉姆看她的艺术作业。

2033
01:18:40.160 --> 01:18:44.960
She has this portfolio, and she's showing him the piece that she got an F on.
她拿着文件夹，给吉姆看那份得了F的作品。

2034
01:18:45.220 --> 01:18:47.640
Oh, I remember shooting this now.
哦，我现在想起来拍过这一段了。

2035
01:18:47.780 --> 01:18:48.320
Yes.
是的。

2036
01:18:48.480 --> 01:18:48.760
Yes.
没错。

2037
01:18:48.960 --> 01:18:50.620
Oh, I remember it.
哦，我记得。

2038
01:18:50.660 --> 01:18:51.840
It's really sweet.
真的很温馨。

2039
01:18:51.840 --> 01:18:58.260
And as he goes through her art assignments, in the back, tucked in the binder, is a sketch pad.
当他翻看她的艺术作业时，在文件夹后面夹着一本素描本。

2040
01:18:58.760 --> 01:19:00.280
And he's like, what is this?
他说，这是什么？

2041
01:19:00.380 --> 01:19:04.220
And she said, oh, you know, it's just sketches of things I would see in New York.
她说，哦，你知道，这只是我在纽约看到的一些东西的素描。

2042
01:19:04.900 --> 01:19:11.520
And when you look at them, Jenna, and I'll put it in stories, it's like people sitting at a cafe, things she might have seen on her walk.
当你看到它们时，珍娜，我会发到故事里，就像人们坐在咖啡馆里，或者是她在散步时看到的东西。

2043
01:19:11.700 --> 01:19:13.100
And they're really good.
它们真的很棒。

2044
01:19:13.520 --> 01:19:15.500
And this is such a wonderful moment.
这是一个非常美妙的时刻。

2045
01:19:15.720 --> 01:19:17.080
I wish it had stayed in.
真希望它能保留下来。

2046
01:19:17.460 --> 01:19:18.640
Sam, can you play the clip?
萨姆，能播放一下片段吗？

2047
01:19:19.720 --> 01:19:20.640
This is my project.
这是我的项目。

2048
01:19:21.660 --> 01:19:23.540
Before we start, how did you fail?
开始之前，你怎么会不及格？

2049
01:19:24.060 --> 01:19:25.100
You're good at art.
你很擅长艺术啊。

2050
01:19:26.240 --> 01:19:26.640
See?
你看？

2051
01:19:27.160 --> 01:19:27.560
Yeah.
是啊。

2052
01:19:27.760 --> 01:19:29.580
We had to make a logo for a coffee company.
我们当时得为一家咖啡公司设计标志。

2053
01:19:29.700 --> 01:19:30.160
Well, that's nice.
嗯，那挺好的。

2054
01:19:30.360 --> 01:19:31.320
This is the one that got an A.
这是那个拿了A的作品。

2055
01:19:31.400 --> 01:19:32.400
The teacher handed it out.
老师把它发下来了。

2056
01:19:32.420 --> 01:19:32.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2057
01:19:32.860 --> 01:19:34.000
And this is mine.
而这是我的。

2058
01:19:34.440 --> 01:19:34.960
Well, that's cool.
嗯，那挺酷的。

2059
01:19:35.200 --> 01:19:37.300
I couldn't get it to print out right, so I got an F.
我没能把它打印好，所以拿了个F。

2060
01:19:37.760 --> 01:19:38.680
I would have given you a D.
我会给你个D。

2061
01:19:39.160 --> 01:19:40.980
That's only because we were sleeping with the professor.
那只是因为我们当时和教授有一腿。

2062
01:19:42.220 --> 01:19:43.040
These are cool.
这些很酷。

2063
01:19:44.540 --> 01:19:45.200
What's this?
这是什么？

2064
01:19:45.880 --> 01:19:46.900
That's my sketchbook.
那是我的速写本。

2065
01:19:47.300 --> 01:19:49.360
It's just, you know, stuff I saw in New York.
就是，你知道的，我在纽约看到的一些东西。

2066
01:19:49.560 --> 01:19:50.240
People on the subway.
地铁上的人们。

2067
01:19:50.900 --> 01:19:51.300
Whoa.
哇。

2068
01:19:52.200 --> 01:19:53.580
This is great.
这太棒了。

2069
01:19:53.940 --> 01:19:55.880
It's so much different than your other work.
这和你之前的作品很不一样。

2070
01:19:56.640 --> 01:19:57.660
Wow, Pam.
哇，帕姆。

2071
01:19:58.580 --> 01:19:59.900
That is awesome.
这太厉害了。

2072
01:20:00.640 --> 01:20:01.120
Yeah?
是吗？

2073
01:20:03.220 --> 01:20:03.700
Yeah.
是啊。

2074
01:20:05.120 --> 01:20:06.720
Oh, I wish that had stayed in.
噢，我真希望那段没被剪掉。

2075
01:20:06.720 --> 01:20:13.820
It's a really sweet scene, and I feel like it just shows what Pam did get out of New York,
那是一个非常温馨的场景，我觉得它展现了帕姆在纽约到底收获了什么，

2076
01:20:13.820 --> 01:20:16.000
and I really wish it had been in the episode.
我真的很希望它能出现在正片里。

2077
01:20:16.180 --> 01:20:20.820
I agree, because I don't think Pam's art story is over yet.
我同意，因为我觉得帕姆的艺术故事还没结束。

2078
01:20:21.020 --> 01:20:21.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2079
01:20:21.420 --> 01:20:30.600
You know, she did not have the benefit of, I think, parents or role models who encouraged
你知道，她没有那种能鼓励她去追寻自我这一面的父母或榜样，

2080
01:20:30.600 --> 01:20:37.620
her to follow this piece of herself, and she only finally does now have that person in Jim.
而她现在终于有了吉姆作为那个人。

2081
01:20:37.800 --> 01:20:38.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2082
01:20:38.260 --> 01:20:43.440
So she's going to have to take her art journey at the same time as her romantic journey.
所以她得同时开启她的艺术之旅和浪漫之旅。

2083
01:20:43.800 --> 01:20:47.160
Well, I'm going to put that scene in stories, because it's really sweet.
好吧，我会把那个场景放进故事里，因为它真的很温馨。

2084
01:20:47.320 --> 01:20:48.300
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

2085
01:20:48.400 --> 01:20:49.080
I did, too.
我也是。

2086
01:20:49.080 --> 01:20:51.520
Well, that kind of wraps up this episode.
好了，这集的内容就到这里。

2087
01:20:51.800 --> 01:20:52.120
Yeah.
是啊。

2088
01:20:52.460 --> 01:20:55.380
Thank you to everyone who helped us make this episode.
感谢所有帮助我们制作这一集的人。

2089
01:20:55.560 --> 01:20:55.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2090
01:20:55.960 --> 01:21:02.280
Brent Forrester, Randy Cordray, Wendy McClendon-Covey, and Rich Sommer, thanks for coming on for
布伦特·福雷斯特、兰迪·科德雷、温迪·麦克伦登-考薇和里奇·索莫，感谢你们来参加

2091
01:21:02.280 --> 01:21:02.840
an interview.
采访。

2092
01:21:03.120 --> 01:21:04.360
It takes a village.
这需要众人的力量。

2093
01:21:04.520 --> 01:21:04.960
It does.
确实。

2094
01:21:05.120 --> 01:21:09.320
And thank you to you guys for sending in awesome questions and Winnipeg trivia.
也感谢你们发来很棒的问题和关于温尼伯的冷知识。

2095
01:21:09.700 --> 01:21:10.120
Yes.
是的。

2096
01:21:10.360 --> 01:21:12.120
Some last parting advice.
最后再给点建议。

2097
01:21:12.520 --> 01:21:17.000
According to Andy, Long Island iced teas are way stronger in Canada.
根据安迪所说，长岛冰茶在加拿大的后劲大得多。

2098
01:21:17.000 --> 01:21:20.140
So be careful the next time you order one of those.
所以下次点这种酒的时候要小心点。

2099
01:21:20.480 --> 01:21:21.040
Yes.
是的。

2100
01:21:21.580 --> 01:21:22.760
All right, you guys.
好了，各位。

2101
01:21:23.000 --> 01:21:26.540
Well, that was Business Trip, and we will be seeing you next week.
好了，以上就是《出差》这一集，我们下周再见。

2102
01:21:26.740 --> 01:21:28.040
Yeah, see you next week.
没错，下周见。

2103
